WEBVTT

00:01:31.360 --> 00:01:33.570
Mom, hey, it's me.

00:01:34.070 --> 00:01:35.650
So, about my company's money...

00:01:36.530 --> 00:01:38.490
Yeah, that's right...

00:01:39.620 --> 00:01:41.080
I'm in a real bind.

00:01:41.240 --> 00:01:43.790
Pretending to be someone's relative
in order to swindle them...!

00:01:43.790 --> 00:01:48.120
The Offices of Enma hereby sentence you
to the Realm of Dead Hope!

00:01:50.290 --> 00:01:52.840
Alright, that concludes the study tour of the trial.

00:01:53.550 --> 00:01:55.010
Were you able to take some notes?

00:01:55.170 --> 00:01:56.130
Yes, sir!

00:01:56.720 --> 00:01:57.800
Taking notes is essential.

00:01:57.800 --> 00:01:58.720
Yes, sir!

00:02:00.350 --> 00:02:01.970
They've really grown, haven't they?

00:02:01.970 --> 00:02:06.270
It's the same with any group of newcomers,
but each year I'm filled with emotion...

00:02:06.770 --> 00:02:08.980
Before I even know it... they've grown.

00:02:10.150 --> 00:02:12.020
Next, it's time to get ready
for the employment examination!

00:02:12.400 --> 00:02:13.480
We're gonna do this quickly!

00:02:13.820 --> 00:02:14.780
Yes, sir!

00:02:18.150 --> 00:02:21.450
The Day-to-Day at the Offices of Enma

00:02:22.620 --> 00:02:25.410
So we're holding another employment examination...

00:02:25.580 --> 00:02:28.040
The dead never stop arriving, after all.

00:02:28.410 --> 00:02:30.630
Hell is always understaffed.

00:02:31.130 --> 00:02:36.510
How true. Day after day we're so busy,
I'd take any help we can get.

00:02:37.010 --> 00:02:40.010
Mr. Hozuki, it's about time for the interviews.

00:02:40.390 --> 00:02:42.850
Off you go now, Hozuki.

00:02:43.050 --> 00:02:43.760
Okay.

00:02:49.480 --> 00:02:51.900
HELL MINION
EMPLOYMENT
EXAMINATION
INTERVIEWS

00:02:54.610 --> 00:02:58.110
U-um... What's with his huge cat...?

00:02:59.490 --> 00:03:02.410
HOZUKI
MUSTARD
STRIPPING
HAG

00:03:00.780 --> 00:03:02.370
This is a stress interview.

00:03:03.490 --> 00:03:05.950
I don't think this is the correct meaning of "stress,"

00:03:05.950 --> 00:03:08.750
but I'll keep quiet because
I don't want to hurt my chances of a job offer.

00:03:09.580 --> 00:03:15.040
I'm Kasha, you see. By nature, I'm a monster cat
who eats corpses found in the Mundane World.

00:03:15.840 --> 00:03:20.590
I was a fiend who'd find a funeral, set my sights
on its procession, and then head straight for it.

00:03:21.090 --> 00:03:22.590
A cat in full fling.

00:03:23.300 --> 00:03:27.810
But, as you can see, I'm working in Hell now.

00:03:24.760 --> 00:03:31.140
KASHA
HOZUKI
STRIPPING
HAG

00:03:27.810 --> 00:03:29.770
He's a veteran of the Welcoming Committee.

00:03:30.100 --> 00:03:34.940
To start out, I wanted to see how startled you'd be
when confronted with this unusual situation.

00:03:39.280 --> 00:03:41.280
Well then, let's begin the interview.

00:03:41.700 --> 00:03:46.030
What department would you like to be appointed to
and what kind of job would you like to do there?

00:03:46.330 --> 00:03:50.580
Well, I'd like to work as a torturer in Repeated Lives Hell.

00:03:50.790 --> 00:03:54.080
There are many dead who've received
the lightest sentence and ended up there,

00:03:54.080 --> 00:03:56.340
so I think it's a job worth doing.

00:03:57.130 --> 00:04:00.720
Seems he's got some basic knowledge.
Well, I suppose I'm impressed.

00:04:00.840 --> 00:04:03.260
ZASHIKI
WARASHI

00:04:01.130 --> 00:04:02.760
Write, write, write, write...

00:04:02.760 --> 00:04:03.340
Yeah.

00:04:04.050 --> 00:04:06.970
And what kind of instrument of torture
would you like to use?

00:04:07.310 --> 00:04:10.930
MUSTARD

00:04:07.470 --> 00:04:09.220
Sniff, sniff, sniff...

00:04:09.520 --> 00:04:10.930
What's this smell?

00:04:11.850 --> 00:04:14.560
That man already has a weapon, you know.

00:04:15.230 --> 00:04:17.020
Will you show it to me?

00:04:17.570 --> 00:04:18.570
Of course!

00:04:19.570 --> 00:04:21.240
I would like to use...

00:04:22.650 --> 00:04:25.620
this homemade device
for automatically cutting nails to the quick!

00:04:25.780 --> 00:04:26.820
The position is yours.

00:04:31.250 --> 00:04:34.040
You sure that's a good move?
That guy's a real idiot, you know.

00:04:34.540 --> 00:04:37.000
A fine line separates idiots from geniuses.

00:04:37.750 --> 00:04:40.670
Does that mean it's advantageous to employ idiots?

00:04:40.670 --> 00:04:44.720
Not at all, but complete idiots are not to be trifled with.

00:04:44.840 --> 00:04:47.510
WAITING
ROOM

00:04:46.220 --> 00:04:47.510
Next person, please.

00:04:48.350 --> 00:04:52.770
From serving tea to giving shoulder rubs, I'll do whatever!

00:04:53.600 --> 00:04:56.850
Trying to deceive with her looks like that...
What a shameless woman.

00:04:56.850 --> 00:05:01.480
It's fine. Mortal Hell is in dire need
of a beautiful woman, you see.

00:05:01.650 --> 00:05:02.490
PASS

00:05:02.900 --> 00:05:05.530
So employing people
based on their appearance is a thing, huh?

00:05:06.110 --> 00:05:08.490
WAITING
ROOM

00:05:06.860 --> 00:05:08.160
Next person, please.

00:05:10.240 --> 00:05:12.950
My hobbies are reading and bonsai.

00:05:13.620 --> 00:05:15.870
You've got a scary face, so I'll employ you.

00:05:16.580 --> 00:05:18.710
You sure about that? He said "bonsai," you know?

00:05:18.960 --> 00:05:21.460
Once again employing someone
based on their appearance, huh?

00:05:21.550 --> 00:05:23.880
ZASHIKI
WARASHI

00:05:21.750 --> 00:05:24.090
Write, write, write, write...

00:05:24.590 --> 00:05:26.840
The hell minion animals are next, huh?

00:05:27.050 --> 00:05:31.390
STRIPPING
HAG
MUSTARD
HOZUKI
KASHA

00:05:27.260 --> 00:05:27.890
Yes.

00:05:29.970 --> 00:05:31.470
But, you know...

00:05:31.510 --> 00:05:34.890
HELL MINION
EMPLOYMENT
EXAMINATION
INTERVIEWS

00:05:31.970 --> 00:05:34.770
Animals can't tout their cuteness, okay?

00:05:35.640 --> 00:05:38.350
He won't be paying attention to that, so just act naturally.

00:05:38.770 --> 00:05:42.190
You really can't help putting on
a senpai-like air, can you?

00:05:42.440 --> 00:05:46.900
Oh? Me? Well, I was head hunted away
from my previous position, after all.

00:05:47.070 --> 00:05:49.160
That was just regular mid-career recruitment.

00:05:49.740 --> 00:05:53.870
Dogs of hell, even if it's just an act,
show your canine teeth, slobber,

00:05:53.870 --> 00:05:56.160
and really play up your feral side, alright?

00:05:57.620 --> 00:06:01.500
Shiro, there's no need to be feeding them
that kind of information beforehand.

00:06:01.710 --> 00:06:03.210
Ah, Mr. Hozuki!

00:06:03.420 --> 00:06:05.800
Everyone, please just act naturally.

00:06:06.470 --> 00:06:12.810
That said, I suppose that might be difficult now,
so please bite down on this pressure measurement film.

00:06:13.310 --> 00:06:19.560
HELL MINION
EMPLOYMENT
EXAMINATION
INTERVIEWS

00:06:13.720 --> 00:06:17.850
If you demonstrate sufficient jaw strength
and show purpose in your eyes, I'll employ you.

00:06:17.980 --> 00:06:21.980
Based on those criteria,
wouldn't you be better off employing a shark?

00:06:21.980 --> 00:06:24.280
Or perhaps a Nile crocodile.

00:06:24.570 --> 00:06:31.410
KASHA
HOZUKI
MUSTARD
STRIPPING
HAG

00:06:25.650 --> 00:06:29.660
This is the famous rabbit from Crackling Mountain.

00:06:29.660 --> 00:06:31.450
I'm a Hell minion now.

00:06:31.570 --> 00:06:37.040
MUSTARD

00:06:31.950 --> 00:06:36.790
If you were to take revenge against
your most hated adversary, what would you do?

00:06:37.620 --> 00:06:43.460
I'd imprison them in somewhere dark and smelly,
and I'd let them out 24 hours after they start groaning.

00:06:43.460 --> 00:06:45.460
Then I'd intently stare into their eyes.

00:06:45.880 --> 00:06:55.470
KASHA
HOZUKI
MUSTARD
STRIPPING

00:06:45.880 --> 00:06:55.470
HAG

00:06:46.010 --> 00:06:48.630
He clearly had someone in mind...

00:06:49.340 --> 00:06:51.470
What happened between the two of them?

00:06:51.640 --> 00:06:53.640
Seems pretty deep-seated, huh?

00:06:53.640 --> 00:06:55.140
I rather like it.

00:06:55.810 --> 00:06:57.100
I'll employ you.

00:06:56.850 --> 00:06:57.350
PASS

00:06:57.520 --> 00:06:58.390
Huh?

00:06:59.140 --> 00:07:01.940
If you have any questions, I'll answer them.

00:07:02.650 --> 00:07:06.280
I heard that the Offices of Enma
are a rather unforgiving place,

00:07:06.570 --> 00:07:10.070
so I suppose the fact you've selected me,
came as a surprise...

00:07:11.360 --> 00:07:14.080
It's after you join up, that it becomes unforgiving...

00:07:14.990 --> 00:07:21.670
HOZUKI
MUSTARD
STRIPPING
HAG

00:07:15.330 --> 00:07:17.950
Moreso than the Offices of Enma being unforgiving...

00:07:17.950 --> 00:07:19.750
...is this man here.

00:07:19.910 --> 00:07:21.580
Meow-ha!

00:07:22.290 --> 00:07:27.090
It is my duty to put the right person in the right post,
so don't you worry about that.

00:07:27.710 --> 00:07:32.640
Karauri, Nasubi, please see
to guiding this year's newcomers.

00:07:33.260 --> 00:07:33.970
Okay!
Sure!

00:07:33.970 --> 00:07:34.350
Sure!

00:07:36.760 --> 00:07:38.020
Good morning.

00:07:38.020 --> 00:07:39.140
Mornin'!

00:07:39.140 --> 00:07:40.480
Good morning!

00:07:41.270 --> 00:07:43.190
You will now clean the courtroom.

00:07:43.600 --> 00:07:47.190
After that, you'll head to the records department
and receive today's allotment of documents.

00:07:47.900 --> 00:07:52.820
You'll put those on Mr. Hozuki's desk -
oh, and don't place them there all haphazardly.

00:07:52.820 --> 00:07:53.530
Caramel... Heavenly.

00:07:53.530 --> 00:07:56.280
Line up all the corners of the documents
and make sure they're facing the same way.
Caramel... Heavenly.

00:07:56.280 --> 00:07:56.780
Caramel... Heavenly.

00:07:56.780 --> 00:07:57.490
Then, you'll all take weapons of your choosing
from the arsenal and carry them to each execution site.
Caramel... Heavenly.

00:07:57.490 --> 00:07:58.200
Then, you'll all take weapons of your choosing
from the arsenal and carry them to each execution site.

00:07:58.200 --> 00:08:00.960
Then, you'll all take weapons of your choosing
from the arsenal and carry them to each execution site.
Yo-heave-ho! Yo-heave-ho! Yo-heave-ho!

00:08:00.960 --> 00:08:01.750
For a start, you'll be doing
that same routine each morning.
Yo-heave-ho! Yo-heave-ho! Yo-heave-ho!

00:08:01.750 --> 00:08:03.670
For a start, you'll be doing
that same routine each morning.
I have work for the time being,

00:08:03.670 --> 00:08:05.790
Where's the arsenal?
but I'll need to compete with drones soon...

00:08:05.790 --> 00:08:06.960
At the end of the East Building.

00:08:07.250 --> 00:08:08.710
That's the third time I've told you.

00:08:09.760 --> 00:08:14.090
Not asking is a problem, but it's not good
to have to ask the same thing too many times either.

00:08:14.340 --> 00:08:16.100
Karauri, Nasubi.

00:08:16.550 --> 00:08:17.300
Okay!
Sure!

00:08:18.510 --> 00:08:21.140
Alright, now please try and do everything I've told you to.

00:08:21.140 --> 00:08:21.930
Yes, sir!

00:08:23.140 --> 00:08:25.310
Mr. Karauri sure is shrewd.

00:08:25.860 --> 00:08:27.730
I wonder if I'll be able to become like that...

00:08:29.730 --> 00:08:33.490
I see that acting as the new arrivals' senpai
has become second nature for you two.

00:08:35.820 --> 00:08:36.700
Huh?

00:08:37.490 --> 00:08:39.910
Please produce a clean copy of the trial records.

00:08:40.040 --> 00:08:42.460
Oh, that's a crucial duty of the records department.

00:08:43.250 --> 00:08:46.250
SENTENCE -  REALM OF DEAD HOPE

00:08:43.580 --> 00:08:46.000
Sentenced to... the Realm of Dead Hope?

00:08:46.960 --> 00:08:49.500
The trial we observed yesterday
had that same sentence, didn't it?

00:08:50.380 --> 00:08:52.630
The nature of the offenses mostly have to deal with fraud.

00:08:53.130 --> 00:08:56.050
Nowadays, there are both telephones
and the Internet, after all.

00:08:56.470 --> 00:08:58.720
Fraud has been present throughout the ages.

00:08:59.140 --> 00:09:00.310
Long ago...

00:09:01.600 --> 00:09:05.310
G-Gosaku? Is that really you, Gosaku?!

00:09:05.310 --> 00:09:08.230
It sure is! Mom, it's me!

00:09:08.690 --> 00:09:10.270
"Mom, it's me."

00:09:10.690 --> 00:09:14.570
There was lots of fraud in which someone would claim
to be a loved one who's back after 10 years away.

00:09:15.070 --> 00:09:16.950
There were no photographs in those days, after all.

00:09:17.570 --> 00:09:19.490
Even mothers would get tricked.

00:09:19.870 --> 00:09:21.040
I see...

00:09:21.290 --> 00:09:25.750
Uh, you know, it seems there's been some
"it's me" fraud in Hell recently.

00:09:26.120 --> 00:09:28.040
Not too long ago, my own mom-

00:09:28.040 --> 00:09:28.920
She was targeted?!

00:09:30.250 --> 00:09:31.000
Yeah.

00:09:34.720 --> 00:09:36.470
Yes? Hello.

00:09:36.970 --> 00:09:39.220
Ah, Mother. It's me - me.

00:09:41.970 --> 00:09:44.640
I'm telling you it's me. You listening, Mother?

00:09:44.640 --> 00:09:45.980
My little Non?

00:09:46.100 --> 00:09:49.520
That's right. Ah, my voice might sound
a little weird 'cause I've got a cold right now.

00:09:49.520 --> 00:09:51.150
So, you see, the thing is-

00:09:52.530 --> 00:09:55.780
You know, I don't even have a child named "Non."

00:09:56.400 --> 00:10:00.120
I never call her "Mother,"
so she said she figured it out right away.

00:10:00.120 --> 00:10:03.410
She may not look it, but your mom is quite courageous.

00:10:03.410 --> 00:10:06.960
Well, the very fact she's married to a ghostly oxen cart...

00:10:07.580 --> 00:10:11.500
But, I suppose it's a good idea to call the person
by a nickname you normally never use for them.

00:10:11.750 --> 00:10:13.500
To trick them into revealing the truth, huh?

00:10:14.130 --> 00:10:16.760
People often suggest creating
some kind of secret word ahead of time.

00:10:17.010 --> 00:10:20.300
But, you know, when the need arises I bet I'd forget it.

00:10:20.300 --> 00:10:23.220
It'd also be pain for a parent and child
to say it every single time...

00:10:23.220 --> 00:10:24.140
Yeah.

00:10:24.720 --> 00:10:26.560
Well, there is another option.

00:10:27.020 --> 00:10:28.640
Right at the start of the conversation...

00:10:29.060 --> 00:10:32.570
Oh, that you, Kenji? If it's money you want,
I'm not giving you any.

00:10:33.520 --> 00:10:35.190
Just say something like that.

00:10:35.530 --> 00:10:39.660
That's... fine if it's a swindler, but that's
a rough thing to say between parent and child.

00:10:40.320 --> 00:10:43.910
Ms. Stripping Hag, no matter
who she's talking to on the phone, always...

00:10:43.910 --> 00:10:46.500
What? That you, Jizobo?

00:10:46.870 --> 00:10:51.380
Hey, send me some money! Money! Money, you hear?!

00:10:51.380 --> 00:10:52.880
...starts the conversation that way.

00:10:53.460 --> 00:10:56.670
I don't think anyone would be able
to get any money off her.

00:10:57.090 --> 00:10:58.760
Isn't she just a regular old hag?

00:10:59.090 --> 00:11:00.090
She's scary...

00:11:01.140 --> 00:11:02.970
Well, guess everyone has a different take.

00:11:03.800 --> 00:11:08.230
No matter who the swindler feigns to be,
once they phone Mr. Hozuki...

00:11:09.140 --> 00:11:11.560
You used the company's money, you say?

00:11:12.940 --> 00:11:14.730
Bear the responsibility on your own.

00:11:16.320 --> 00:11:18.030
...seems like he'd say that and hang up.

00:11:19.200 --> 00:11:24.160
But, the Stripping Hag seems like she'd fall for it
if someone says they have a great way to make money.

00:11:24.740 --> 00:11:27.160
Don't take the Stripping Hag so lightly.

00:11:27.910 --> 00:11:32.540
Got it. I'll double it for you, so come on
and give me 5 million yen as seed money.

00:11:32.830 --> 00:11:37.380
Come on, give it to me. Hurry up and give it here.

00:11:38.710 --> 00:11:39.880
That's what she'd say.

00:11:40.720 --> 00:11:42.380
I guess old hags really are shrewd...

00:11:43.010 --> 00:11:45.260
She has no thought of covering for her relatives,

00:11:45.260 --> 00:11:48.060
and she doesn't want any part in an investment
that requires paying with her own money.

00:11:48.390 --> 00:11:50.810
Is she being reasonable, or is she just scum?

00:11:51.890 --> 00:11:53.560
But that is just it.

00:11:54.230 --> 00:12:00.320
The feeling of wanting to keep the shame of one's
relatives under wraps, surely encourages "it's me" fraud.

00:12:01.030 --> 00:12:04.200
Which is why the hells for such fraud
are not going anywhere.

00:12:04.200 --> 00:12:08.040
Indeed. But Internet scams
are especially prevalent right now.

00:12:09.580 --> 00:12:16.710
TURN GOODS INTO MONEY
LICKETY-SPLIT

00:12:09.910 --> 00:12:12.790
Like, the ones that tell you to pay up
when you click on something...

00:12:12.790 --> 00:12:16.460
Humans really do think up one thing after the next...

00:12:17.210 --> 00:12:19.840
Hell is trying to deal with the issue at a rapid pace,

00:12:20.670 --> 00:12:26.010
but even now yokai are like,
"Let's sumo wrestle!" Before long...

00:12:26.510 --> 00:12:28.810
Note: A "shirikodama" is a mythical ball inside the anus that kappa seek
to obtain.
Put your shirikodama on the line and let's wrestle!

00:12:28.810 --> 00:12:30.310
Rather than that, it will be...

00:12:31.180 --> 00:12:33.480
Let's battle each other online.

00:12:33.810 --> 00:12:36.440
This is an era in which
we have to deal with things like that.

00:12:38.730 --> 00:12:41.650
Well, be that as it may, please go do your jobs.

00:12:41.650 --> 00:12:42.860
Oh, that's right.
Sure!

00:12:43.110 --> 00:12:44.200
Mr. Karauri!

00:12:45.030 --> 00:12:46.990
We've done all that we were instructed to.

00:12:47.320 --> 00:12:49.790
Much appreciated. I'll inspect your work.

00:12:50.370 --> 00:12:52.500
So, what should we do next?

00:12:52.790 --> 00:12:54.250
Ah, perfect timing.

00:12:54.790 --> 00:12:57.420
Come to the record department with me
and sort the documents.

00:12:58.000 --> 00:13:01.130
Organizing the documents there
takes a whole day, you see.

00:13:01.630 --> 00:13:05.260
I'm in the process of producing this clean copy,
so you should also watch me as I work.

00:13:05.260 --> 00:13:06.050
Yes, sir!

00:13:06.510 --> 00:13:09.100
SENTENCE-  REALM OF DEAD HOPE

00:13:07.050 --> 00:13:11.140
"The Realm of Dead Hope"...? What kind of place is that?

00:13:11.850 --> 00:13:16.440
That's the hell you go to when you pretend
to be someone else in order to deceive people.

00:13:17.860 --> 00:13:21.360
If I remember right, a long time ago it was the hell
for those who posed as monks to swindle people.

00:13:22.440 --> 00:13:23.490
Isn't that right?

00:13:24.530 --> 00:13:26.450
Is that where all people who commit fraud go?

00:13:26.570 --> 00:13:27.320
Nope!

00:13:27.660 --> 00:13:29.530
Let's see... There are other places, too.

00:13:30.530 --> 00:13:34.290
If you take something by deceptive means
and sell it, or dodge taxes or embezzle funds,

00:13:34.290 --> 00:13:35.830
you go to the Canine Mauling Realm.

00:13:37.920 --> 00:13:40.960
If you use deceptive means to confiscate land,
that's the Fiery Forging Realm.

00:13:41.840 --> 00:13:45.380
It's evidence that these minute distinctions
in fraud have existed since long ago.

00:13:45.760 --> 00:13:48.590
Amazing! You really know your stuff!

00:13:48.590 --> 00:13:50.760
O-o-oh, I wouldn't say that!

00:13:51.810 --> 00:13:54.020
Anyway, that's right, isn't it? I'm correct, aren't I?

00:13:54.180 --> 00:13:56.770
Amazing! Those are such detailed notes!

00:13:57.140 --> 00:14:01.110
I'm not very good at taking notes myself...
That won't do, will it?

00:14:01.110 --> 00:14:05.190
I take notes, but I tend to forget to look over them.

00:14:05.570 --> 00:14:07.910
Everybody deals with that kind of stuff
when they're just starting out.

00:14:07.910 --> 00:14:10.410
Personally, I was a real piece of junk at first.

00:14:10.620 --> 00:14:12.790
Even now, I still commit blunders.

00:14:13.200 --> 00:14:16.750
I mean, of the various 16 mini hells,
I only have grasp of about half of them.

00:14:17.210 --> 00:14:17.870
Right?

00:14:20.960 --> 00:14:23.800
Wow... Amazing...

00:14:24.630 --> 00:14:29.550
The very fact you claim the title of "senpai" is fraud.
How'd you manage to pass the interview?

00:14:30.550 --> 00:14:32.010
By just being myself.

00:14:38.270 --> 00:14:40.440
HELLISH RESTAURANT
UNCOUTH-DINING YAKSHA
10-YEAR ANNIVERSARY
LARGE SERVING
EAT IT ALL WITHIN 20 MINUTES AND IT'S FREE!
PREMIUM COURSE

00:14:38.270 --> 00:14:40.440
STANDARD COURSE

00:14:38.310 --> 00:14:40.440
LOOK FORWARD TO SEEING
WHAT'S IN THE HELL DISH!
SPECIAL COURSE

00:14:40.440 --> 00:14:42.060
LARGE SERVING
EAT IT ALL WITHIN 20 MINUTES AND IT'S FREE!

00:14:49.450 --> 00:14:50.820
FREE

00:14:58.460 --> 00:15:01.710
1 Soup, 3 Dishes, 10 Meats

00:15:05.250 --> 00:15:08.380
Speaking of stuff that "totally happens"
with owners, THAT is definitely on the list.

00:15:08.630 --> 00:15:11.090
What a wittle cutie!

00:15:11.090 --> 00:15:12.890
Is that wummy?

00:15:12.890 --> 00:15:14.390
Is it wummy in your tummy?

00:15:14.890 --> 00:15:16.810
Know what I mean by "when he admires me,
he makes an unexpectedly absurd face"?

00:15:14.930 --> 00:15:16.810
It is yummy?

00:15:16.810 --> 00:15:19.140
Know what I mean by "when he admires me,
he makes an unexpectedly absurd face"?

00:15:19.560 --> 00:15:21.440
Yeah, that totally happens.

00:15:21.440 --> 00:15:23.560
I do feel my owner's love, though.

00:15:23.690 --> 00:15:26.070
They sure get all close while making a ridiculous face!

00:15:26.070 --> 00:15:28.690
Also, they give you too many treats and you get fat.

00:15:28.690 --> 00:15:30.200
Yeah, totally happens.

00:15:30.740 --> 00:15:33.530
My owner also used to shower me with love.

00:15:33.870 --> 00:15:37.290
All of you had pretty darn nice homes, huh?

00:15:38.040 --> 00:15:39.370
LOOK!

00:15:40.160 --> 00:15:41.500
Look! Look!

00:15:41.500 --> 00:15:42.420
What? What?!

00:15:42.790 --> 00:15:44.330
Look! Isn't this amazing?!

00:15:45.380 --> 00:15:48.210
"Large Serving. Eat it all within 20 minutes and it's free"?

00:15:48.550 --> 00:15:49.510
"Free"?!

00:15:50.220 --> 00:15:54.760
Oh, that's right, we had a gluttonous dog
like Shiro here among us this whole time.

00:15:55.260 --> 00:15:56.890
Huh? What are you talking about?

00:15:57.010 --> 00:15:58.060
"Gluttonous"?

00:15:58.180 --> 00:16:00.480
Hey... you're gonna get fat again.

00:16:00.640 --> 00:16:03.310
Dogs are best when they're a little chubby, alright?!

00:16:03.560 --> 00:16:06.860
Isn't that a cliché uttered by owners of fat dogs?!

00:16:07.020 --> 00:16:10.030
Both the gluttonous dog I'm talking about
and their owner said that same thing!

00:16:10.110 --> 00:16:11.820
SHUT UP, CORGI!

00:16:11.820 --> 00:16:15.410
Given your breed's naturally plump bodies,
you're the last one I wanna hear that from!

00:16:15.570 --> 00:16:18.330
Nevertheless, this appears to be quite a lavish feast.

00:16:18.330 --> 00:16:20.660
This special course here looks good to me!

00:16:20.950 --> 00:16:22.040
The meat, huh?

00:16:22.710 --> 00:16:26.040
I am curious about the premium course's "Hell Dish"...

00:16:26.460 --> 00:16:29.380
but the standard course's red rice
with high-grade adzuki beans

00:16:29.380 --> 00:16:32.380
and a large serving of red bean soup
also sounds like a dreadful combination.

00:16:32.380 --> 00:16:33.970
Bet it'd give you heartburn.

00:16:34.300 --> 00:16:35.090
"Red rice"?!

00:16:35.090 --> 00:16:36.220
"Red bean soup"?!

00:16:37.640 --> 00:16:41.480
Eeeeek!

00:16:42.810 --> 00:16:47.150
Oh, that's right, adzuki-bean dishes
are a favorite of the Zashiki Warashi, aren't they?

00:16:47.690 --> 00:16:50.030
Mr. Hozuki!

00:16:50.030 --> 00:16:51.860
Take me to this place!

00:16:51.860 --> 00:16:55.860
Why are they trying to get Mr. Hozuki to take them there?

00:16:56.530 --> 00:16:58.410
In short, there could be only one reason...

00:16:58.410 --> 00:17:01.830
They want him to pay their bill if they're
unable to finish their meals, right?

00:17:02.370 --> 00:17:04.250
HELLISH RESTAURANT
UNCOUTH-DINING YAKSHA

00:17:04.710 --> 00:17:06.120
So this is the place, huh?

00:17:06.120 --> 00:17:07.210
Yay!

00:17:07.830 --> 00:17:09.460
Let me be clear from the start:

00:17:10.380 --> 00:17:13.050
If you don't finish your meal,
you'll have to pay for it yourself.

00:17:13.050 --> 00:17:13.970
'Kay!

00:17:14.220 --> 00:17:15.090
Huh?!

00:17:17.300 --> 00:17:21.640
I should've known... But, then,
why did you come with us anyway?

00:17:21.810 --> 00:17:26.400
Because of the premium course's "Hell Dish" -
I'm curious about it.

00:17:33.240 --> 00:17:35.280
Have you decided on your order?

00:17:35.700 --> 00:17:36.780
Standard course for us.

00:17:37.360 --> 00:17:38.320
Special course for me.

00:17:39.070 --> 00:17:40.120
Premium course for me.

00:17:40.240 --> 00:17:42.830
Oh, you're going for the premium course?

00:17:43.200 --> 00:17:44.080
Yes.

00:17:44.250 --> 00:17:46.710
Put in an order of standard, special, and premium!

00:17:46.710 --> 00:17:47.620
Got it!

00:17:48.000 --> 00:17:50.130
Please wait just a moment.

00:17:50.840 --> 00:17:53.590
My hunger's reaching the breaking point!

00:17:54.460 --> 00:17:56.340
It's best not to drink any water.

00:17:56.590 --> 00:17:59.640
Yep, the rice will expand in your stomach if you do.

00:18:01.050 --> 00:18:02.720
Thanks fer waitin'!

00:18:02.720 --> 00:18:04.310
Here's two orders of the standard dish!

00:18:05.060 --> 00:18:07.440
Wow, that looks super sweet-tasting!

00:18:08.650 --> 00:18:09.940
Here's the special course!

00:18:10.610 --> 00:18:14.280
Amazing! A table mountain made of meat!

00:18:15.240 --> 00:18:16.530
Here's the premium course!

00:18:19.110 --> 00:18:20.910
Huh? What's that...?

00:18:21.370 --> 00:18:22.450
It's swaying.

00:18:23.290 --> 00:18:24.540
It is swaying, isn't it?

00:18:26.200 --> 00:18:31.250
If ya conquer your fear of not knowing what the
premium course is made outta and finish it, it's free!

00:18:31.500 --> 00:18:33.590
Isn't the spirit of the premium course
different than the rest?!

00:18:33.800 --> 00:18:36.260
You alright with that?! That okay with you, Mr. Hozuki?!

00:18:36.260 --> 00:18:37.800
There's a time limit of 20 minutes!

00:18:38.340 --> 00:18:40.510
Well then, all four of you...

00:18:40.800 --> 00:18:42.050
Start!

00:18:44.680 --> 00:18:48.350
Yummy! If nothing else,
this special course's meat is delish!

00:18:49.310 --> 00:18:52.520
I'll be just fine, but the Warashis have rice
and adzuki beans, right?!

00:18:52.520 --> 00:18:53.900
I wonder if they'll be alright...

00:18:58.780 --> 00:19:03.530
H-huh...?! One of them is using the scoop
to shovel rice into the other's mouth?!

00:19:03.530 --> 00:19:06.370
They're like mechanical dolls - scary!

00:19:06.540 --> 00:19:12.790
SNAP
CHOMP
SNAP
CHOMP
SNAP
CHOMP

00:19:06.620 --> 00:19:10.580
S-speaking of that, these girls are actually
a kind of yokai, aren't they?

00:19:10.580 --> 00:19:12.710
Compared to human girls,
the norms they abide by are diff-

00:19:12.710 --> 00:19:14.420
They've switched roles!

00:19:18.760 --> 00:19:19.590
Huh?

00:19:21.470 --> 00:19:23.890
They stopped? Did they reach their limit?

00:19:31.190 --> 00:19:32.150
Uh-huh...

00:19:33.980 --> 00:19:38.280
Now that it's cooled down a bit to a nice temperature,
they downed the  red bean soup in one go!

00:19:38.440 --> 00:19:43.240
Do the Zashiki Warashi consider
red bean soup TO BE A MERE DRINK?!

00:19:49.620 --> 00:19:51.460
Wh-when did he...?!

00:19:51.580 --> 00:19:54.500
What was it?! Mr. Hozuki, what was that?!

00:19:54.750 --> 00:19:55.500
Dunno...

00:19:55.710 --> 00:19:56.840
Was it good?!

00:19:57.460 --> 00:19:59.880
In terms of taste, it was delicious...

00:20:02.090 --> 00:20:03.340
but we still have 10 minutes.

00:20:03.590 --> 00:20:05.100
OH, THAT'S RIGHT!

00:20:06.100 --> 00:20:08.390
Shiro, I see you also eat quite a lot.

00:20:09.430 --> 00:20:10.980
So, it appears that all four of us...

00:20:15.150 --> 00:20:16.610
It's been 20 minutes!

00:20:18.570 --> 00:20:19.650
Amazing!

00:20:19.650 --> 00:20:21.190
You all finished yer meals!

00:20:21.190 --> 00:20:22.700
Huh?! Seriously?!

00:20:22.900 --> 00:20:25.780
I didn't think those girls had any shot at all!

00:20:26.830 --> 00:20:29.240
That dog sure looks stuffed!

00:20:30.080 --> 00:20:33.750
Excuse me, so... what was this anyway?

00:20:33.960 --> 00:20:36.080
The ultimate jellied meat broth.

00:20:36.080 --> 00:20:37.250
"Jellied meat broth"?!

00:20:37.250 --> 00:20:40.050
It's 30,000 yen if you can't finish a platter
of jellied meat broth?!

00:20:40.260 --> 00:20:41.300
Isn't that too expensive?!

00:20:41.800 --> 00:20:47.970
Well, the ingredients include Japanese beef,
swallow's nest, shark fin, top-grade squid ink,

00:20:43.590 --> 00:20:52.930
RARE WATER
SHARK FIN
JAPANESE BEEF
SWALLOW'S NEST

00:20:43.630 --> 00:20:52.930
WOODLOUSE ANTENNA
SQUID INK

00:20:47.970 --> 00:20:53.020
woodlouse antenna, and Black Cord Hell rare water -
the parts of that stuff that're normally discarded.

00:20:53.140 --> 00:20:54.690
This is a "zero yen" restaurant!

00:20:55.600 --> 00:20:57.860
It sounds like supreme-grade Chinese food.

00:20:58.480 --> 00:21:02.360
Still, you did well to eat that amount
of jellied meat broth, Mr. Hozuki.

00:21:02.650 --> 00:21:05.570
In a sense, that's harder than finishing the rice or meat.

00:21:05.910 --> 00:21:07.820
Indeed, it certainly was hard.

00:21:10.160 --> 00:21:11.910
Thank you for the meal.

00:21:12.700 --> 00:21:14.580
Thanks for your patronage!

00:21:14.580 --> 00:21:16.500
That was delicious. Let's come again sometime.

00:21:16.750 --> 00:21:19.000
Let's come again with Mr. Hozuki.

00:21:19.290 --> 00:21:22.380
Ugh... Can I even walk...?

00:21:23.050 --> 00:21:25.840
Oh? What's the matter, Mr. Hozuki?

00:21:25.840 --> 00:21:27.640
Please go home ahead of me.

00:21:27.840 --> 00:21:29.970
Are you gonna puke up
the jellied meat broth or something?

00:21:30.220 --> 00:21:35.480
Nope, to be honest, with the jellied meat broth,
what was hard is that I didn't feel I really ate anything.

00:21:38.650 --> 00:21:39.940
Thanks fer waitin'!

00:21:39.940 --> 00:21:41.900
Here's one order each of the
standard and special courses!

00:21:43.650 --> 00:21:45.950
I'll head home after I have some rice and meat.

00:21:47.320 --> 00:21:50.410
This guy is like one of those mechanical dolls...

00:23:24.960 --> 00:23:26.960
NEXT TIME
ON HOZUKI'S
COOLHEADEDNESS...

00:23:25.880 --> 00:23:27.880
"Miracle"? That's...

00:23:27.880 --> 00:23:30.050
...Ms. Maki's first film appearance.

00:23:28.470 --> 00:23:29.130
AND

00:23:30.340 --> 00:23:33.090
Next, it's up in the air if she'll take on the role
of a clumsy magical girl or not.

00:23:31.550 --> 00:23:32.260
BUT

00:23:33.090 --> 00:23:35.810
Huh? Wearing those Western clothes,
where are you going?

00:23:33.550 --> 00:23:34.510
SO

00:23:35.810 --> 00:23:38.060
To buy Western clothes for the Zashiki Warashi.

00:23:36.470 --> 00:23:39.810
WE PRESENT:
WHAT IS A MAGICAL GIRL?
AND
INDULGING IN WESTERN CLOTHING
PLEASE ENJOY!

00:23:38.060 --> 00:23:39.770
Now THAT'S a miracle.
